plan.prompt:
Stage: plan. Load the game-production skill. Plan the production of this game, in scope and on budget.

<brief>
{{input.brief}}
</brief>
Engine: {{input.engine}}
Dimension: {{input.dimension}}
Genre: {{input.genre}}
Budget: {{input.budget}}
Asset sources allowed: {{input.sources}}

Write .studio/project.json (plugins/games3d/sdk/FORMATS.md: name, engine, dimension, genre, design "design/GDD.md", budgets, stages plan, concept, art, assets, prototype, playtest, vertical-slice, content, polish, build, full-playtest, report, each {"id", "title", "status": "pending"}; plan "done") and design/production-plan.md: the first version's scope and what is cut for later, the starting point (web: the studio_template that fits, from studio_template list; godot: its project.create template 2d, 2.5d or 3d; unreal: its project.create template), the asset list in one line each, the budget (model spend, time) and the risks. Unity is not covered yet: if the engine is unity, say so and stop.
Feedback, if any: {{feedback}}

concept.prompt:
Stage: concept. Load the game-design skill. Write design/GDD.md from the brief and design/production-plan.md with the skill's GDD template: Pitch, Core loop, Controls, Mechanics, Rules (win and lose), Levels, Art direction, Audio, UI, Balancing (the numbers: speeds, jump height in tiles, health, counts), Scope. Make the goal exactly what the game reports as won (web templates: window.__game.won; Godot: StudioHook "won"; Unreal: the kit's win event), and list the state a bot reads (player, score, targets). For Godot add a "Self-test" section. Set the concept stage to "review" in .studio/project.json.

<brief>
{{input.brief}}
</brief>
Engine: {{input.engine}}, dimension: {{input.dimension}}, genre: {{input.genre}}
Feedback, if any (fix exactly this): {{feedback}}

prototype-fix.prompt:
Stage: prototype-fix. The prototype checks failed. Fix the game (never weaken a check; change a test only when the test is wrong, and say why), then play it again with game_bot goal. Test budget: game_bot goal once the mechanic works and once after your last change, not after every edit (the gates play it again); game_play frames at most 3 times in this stage, after a batch of visual changes, not one by one.

The checks that failed, with their evidence:
{{feedback}}

slice-fix.prompt:
Stage: slice-fix. The vertical-slice checks failed. Fix them and play again. Test budget: game_bot goal once the mechanic works and once after your last change, not after every edit (the gates play it again); game_play frames at most 3 times in this stage, after a batch of visual changes, not one by one.

The checks that failed, with their evidence:
{{feedback}}

ui-fix.prompt:
Stage: ui-fix. The content checks failed (levels, screens or wiring). Fix them and play again.

The checks that failed, with their evidence:
{{feedback}}

polish-fix.prompt:
Stage: polish-fix. The polish checks failed. Fix them; run game_playtest again with the goal at the end.

The checks that failed, with their evidence:
{{feedback}}

build-fix.prompt:
Stage: build-fix. The build check failed. Read the build log, fix the cause (missing assets, a broken preset, a cook error), and build again.

The checks that failed, with their evidence:
{{feedback}}
